.Im MicroEmacs variable|window
.so me.tni
.TH $window-id 5
.XI $window-id - "Current window identity"
.XI $window-pid - "Previous window identity"
.SH NAME
.Me "|$window-id"
$window-id \- Current window identity
.br
.Me "|$window-pid"
$window-id \- Previous window identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB$window-id\fR \fIinteger\fR
.br
\fB$window-pid\fR \fIinteger\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fB$window-id\fR retrieves the identity of the current window, this is a integer value (1..n) that is automatically
allocated when a window is created using 
.Ht split-window-horizontally 2
or
.Ht split-window-vertically 2 .
.PP
The \fB$window-id\fR is guaranteed to be unique and is typically used in macros to locate a previous window.
.PP
The \fB$window-pid\fR stores the \fB$window-id\fR of the previous current window, defaulting to 0 if no other window 
has been visited. Note that the window identified by \fB$window-pid\fR may no longer exist so any macro making use of 
this variable must handle the \fIfailed to find\fR case.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.na
.Ht next-window 2 ,
.Ht split-window-horizontally 2 ,
.Ht split-window-vertically 2 ,
.Ht $frame-id 5 .
.ad
.FH
